====================
Mayer-Salvador radii
====================

. R(A.B) = distance from A to a minimum in the ED between
           a pair of 'neighbour' atoms, A and B.

  The . in R(A.B) isn't a bond critical point, but nearly.
  Since it is a minimum in only 1 dimension, not all three.
  A -ve R(A.B) means no minimum in the ED was found -- bad.

. Also reported are R(A.B) for the promolecular density.

. Two atoms are neighbours if their midpoint is *not* closer
  to any third atom. See Salvador & Ramos-Cordoba (2013)
  JCP 139 p. 071103 p3 paragraph 3.

. The radii are used to define Topological Fuzzy Voronoi Atoms
  (TFVAs) i.e. 'Salvador atoms'.



